msgid "Archived Topic: PXFmini Wiring Quick Start"
msgstr "已归档专题：PXFmini 接线快速入门"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:9
#: efd3274e6d47451e9c03e9cbde60e9ff
msgid ""
"PXFmini uses JST-GH connectors instead of DF13. This is the latest "
"adoption made by the DroneCode Foundation"
msgstr "PXFmini 使用 JST-GH 连接器，而非 DF13。这是 DroneCode 基金会最新采用的标准。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:15
#: f747baa6cf4640148adb44600e69a1e7
msgid ""
"This article provides high level information about how to power "
":ref:`PXFmini<common-pxfmini>` and connect its most important "
"peripherals."
msgstr "本文提供 :ref:`PXFmini<common-pxfmini>` 供电及重要外设连接的高层次说明。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:22
#: 04cd9cd5851d46149fc03a58bf06000f
msgid "PXFmini Wiring Chart"
msgstr "PXFmini 接线图"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:30
#: d17d4aecee334becb466323a8853d0a9
msgid "Power PXFmini"
msgstr "PXFmini 供电"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:32
#: 07da5383b8ce4ab49e2694a5cdd4bb5b
msgid ""
"PXFmini is typically powered via its \"power\" port, as shown in the "
"picture below. The power port simultaneously powers PXFmini and reads "
"voltage and current analog measurements."
msgstr "PXFmini 通常通过其「power」接口供电，如下图所示。power 接口同时为 PXFmini 供电并读取电压和电流模拟测量值。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:36
#: 8de0990a79da4c3a8de0b52f42c565e2
msgid ""
"It can be also powered using a BEC, you just need to connect to the PWM "
"rail."
msgstr "也可通过 BEC 供电，只需连接到 PWM 轨即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:38
#: f3ca3f0b9e6d4965a926b4182aaad47c
msgid ""
"Additionally, for developing/configuration purposes, it can be powered "
"using a micro USB charger (2A recommended)."
msgstr "此外，用于开发/配置目的时，可使用 Micro USB 充电器（推荐 2A）供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:48
#: 9f5385dae514457691bf5730824b1331
msgid "Always use a power module to feed PXFmini while flying your drone"
msgstr "飞行时请始终使用电源模块为 PXFmini 供电"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:52
#: d6afed6827274dd7856db43bb4a81e08
msgid "HDMI Connector"
msgstr "HDMI 接口"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:55
#: 7625c852f8934013a4ceee8f6ae3c336
msgid ""
"If you wish to work straight under your Linux based autopilot, you can "
"use the HDMI connector"
msgstr "如果希望直接在基于 Linux 的飞控下工作，可以使用 HDMI 接口"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:55
#: d6aca02be6c2484da0fbf1a366c189eb
msgid "and make your own configurations:"
msgstr "进行自定义配置："

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:62
#: 471ad740799641cdae207e5f90119362
msgid "Connect remote control inputs"
msgstr "连接遥控输入"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:64
#: 0dcc32a03bb14758ab4e8e7af7f440d2
msgid ""
"PXFmini is compatible with PPM remote control (RC) receivers. For "
"traditional single-wire-per-channel (PWM) receivers a PPM encoder can be "
"used to convert the receiver outputs to PPM-SUM."
msgstr "PXFmini 兼容 PPM 遥控（RC）接收机。对于传统的单线多通道（PWM）接收机，可使用 PPM 编码器将接收机输出转换为 PPM-SUM。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:68
#: f88d7dc6fe524121b9626dbd36cab07e
msgid ""
"For more information see :ref:`Compatible RC Transmitter and Receiver "
"Systems (Erle-Brain 2) <common-compatible-rc-transmitter-and-receiver-"
"systems-erle-brain-2>`. The PXFmini is compatible with the tecnology used"
" in Erle-Brain 2."
msgstr ""
"更多信息请参见 :ref:`兼容 RC 发射机和接收机系统（Erle-Brain 2）<common-compatible-rc-"
"transmitter-and-receiver-systems-erle-brain-2>`。PXFmini 与 Erle-Brain 2 "
"所用技术兼容。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:73
#: 09bf3130c8fd4b31842e59ff63598794
msgid "FRSky Taranis Transmitter"
msgstr "FRSky Taranis 遥控器"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:76
#: 11a9dcea3c8340758a05080034537521
msgid "GPS+Compass"
msgstr "GPS+罗盘"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:78
#: f18b0a00e71b459ba9266de34fe69502
msgid ""
"The `uBlox GPS + Compass Module <hhttps://erlerobotics.com/blog/product"
"/gpscompass-ublox-neo-m8n-gps-with-compass-kit/>`__ is the recommended "
"GPS for PXFmini. The GPS port is connected with the six-position DF13 "
"cable, and the Compass port is connected to the I2C port with the four-"
"position JST-GH cable, as shown in the next image:"
msgstr ""
"`uBlox GPS + 罗盘模块 <hhttps://erlerobotics.com/blog/product/gpscompass-"
"ublox-neo-m8n-gps-with-compass-kit/>`__ 是 PXFmini 的推荐 GPS。GPS 接口使用六针 DF13"
" 连接线连接，罗盘接口使用四针 JST-GH 连接线连接到 I2C 接口，如下图所示："

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:87
#: c34661eb5ec041f08dcee52ecd393f06
msgid "Connect Motors"
msgstr "连接电机"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:89
#: fe92263532d441879917cc31b3332520
msgid "Use the PWM rail in order to connect them:"
msgstr "使用 PWM 排针进行连接："

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:96
#: c2652b92415d4bea923a670425fa260d
msgid ""
"Be aware of how you connect ESCs wires to PWM rail. The signal wire "
"(white or orange color) should be connected at the top, the ground wire "
"(black or brown color) at the bottom."
msgstr "连接 ESC 线到 PWM 排针时请注意方向。信号线（白色或橙色）应连接在顶部，地线（黑色或棕色）连接在底部。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:107
#: 5a076d59444b4893a219b6463f8d6507
msgid "USB ports"
msgstr "USB 接口"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:109
#: 0297756ddabc44b7842ea4515e792cea
msgid ""
"You could attach different dongle/devices to the USB ports that includes "
"Raspberry Pi 2/3/Zero:"
msgstr "您可以将各种适配器/设备连接到包括 Raspberry Pi 2/3/Zero 的 USB 接口："

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:113
#: 2578ab35f61848689d4041adb2b4ba54
msgid "WiFi dongle"
msgstr "WiFi 适配器"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:115
#: a9e2a00eeed0417fa0b557d4804ff170
msgid ""
"Use a (regular or high gain) WiFi dongle to create a hotspot that can, "
"for example, be used for sending telemetry data and commands to a Ground "
"Station.  If you use the `images "
"<http://docs.erlerobotics.com/brains/os_images>`__ provided by Erle "
"Robotics, they automatically generate a WiFi hotspot."
msgstr ""
"使用（普通或高增益）WiFi 适配器创建热点，例如用于向地面站发送数传数据和指令。如果您使用 Erle Robotics 提供的 `镜像 "
"<http://docs.erlerobotics.com/brains/os_images>`__，它们会自动生成 WiFi 热点。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:126
#: 3d7d371808624cf795a489c847596152
msgid ""
"Edimax AC (regular and high gain) are the officially supported dongles. "
"These can be purchased from Erle-Brain with your autopilot/vehicle."
msgstr "Edimax AC（普通和高增益）是官方支持的适配器。可在购买飞控/飞行器时从 Erle-Brain 处购买。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:131
#: 3036919202154ae2802387c395e85df8
msgid "Bluetooth dongle"
msgstr "蓝牙适配器"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:133
#: 6779737b5d284d249949cf9235a3c917
msgid "Use a Bluetooth dongle to connect additional devices, such as joysticks."
msgstr "使用蓝牙适配器连接其他设备，如游戏手柄。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:137
#: 1e1a171069c5403888afe60f07174b4e
msgid "You will need to configure BlueTooth interface to make it work"
msgstr "需要配置蓝牙接口才能使其正常工作"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:142
#: 28d8d92aef4540ff96f859fb2b04b351
msgid "Connect other peripherals"
msgstr "连接其他外设"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:144
#: c62e1dcb25f64aa59a7f75a9ddb53690
msgid ""
"Depending on your hardware there may be any number of other peripherals "
"attached, including sensors, cameras, grippers etc. These can be found as"
" sub-pages of the topic :ref:`Optional Hardware <common-optional-"
"hardware>`."
msgstr ""
"根据您的硬件，可能还需要连接传感器、相机、夹持器等各种外设。这些内容可在 :ref:`可选硬件 <common-optional-"
"hardware>` 主题的子页面中找到。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-pxfmini-wiring-quick-start.rst:148
#: dc14785661814c18b5bff81989931414
msgid ""
"More information in `official documentation "
"<http://erlerobotics.com/docs/Artificial_Brains_and_Autopilots/Additional_Sensors/Lidar.html>`__."
msgstr ""
"更多信息请参见 `官方文档 "
"<http://erlerobotics.com/docs/Artificial_Brains_and_Autopilots/Additional_Sensors/Lidar.html>`__。"

